invariant: INV-14
file: srv_quic.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh srv_quic
reason: take_transport_params accepts a ClientHello that carries no
  quic_transport_parameters, which RFC 9001 section 8.2 makes a fatal
  missing_extension alert. The srv_quic proof asserts that such a first
  hello is refused with that alert, and fails on this edit.

--- old
    if (ch->transport_params == NULL) {
        q->hs.alert = ALERT_MISSING_EXTENSION;
        return CH_EPROTO;
    }
    if (q->t.cfg.on_transport_params != NULL) {
--- new
    if (q->t.cfg.on_transport_params != NULL && ch->transport_params != NULL) {
